    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288-a1">

                <pb facs="0464" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg368"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 396.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Lord Salisbury to Mr. Hay.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-05-13"><hi rendition="#italic">May 13,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: With reference to my note of
                    the 7th instant, respecting the United States missionaries in Sierra Leone, I
                    have the satisfaction to inform you that the secretary of state for the colonies
                        <pb facs="0465" n="369" xml:id="pg369"/> has received a telegram from the
                    governor of Sierra Leone from which it appears that the United States
                    missionaries from Robethel are all safe at Freetown.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis Bertie.</hi></signed><lb/>(In
                    the absence of the Marquis of Salisbury.)</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
